if you've played your share of Ubisoft  open-world games you know the deal  revealing the secrets and collectibles  of a given area outpost or district  takes a bit of effort it's a more  layered form of infiltration and  watchdogs hacking CTOs centers isn't  enough you also need to hack the various  CTOs towers within each part of Chicago  the challenge is in gaining access to  these fenced in towers these spatial  puzzles are some of the best brain  teasers in watchdogs but if you do find  yourself stumped here's a collection of  walkthrough videos to guide you to each  tower mad mile Northwest approaching  from the north head down a wide alley  leading to the courtyard while still on  the ground level look for an unlock  panel after hacking the panel had  further down the alley and used the lift  to your right climb until you reach the  roof then look for a small glass bridge  cross it but before you hop the fence  make a 180-degree turn to find another  unlocked animal now hop the fence go  through the CTOs gate and make a right  cross the glass bridge walk across the  roof and hop over the railing to reach  the tower  parker's square east this tower puzzle  serves as a reminder that forklifts and  other movable objects occasionally hide  cameras from view when you're within the  fence of the facility hack into the  first available camera then hack the  forklift to reveal another camera this  camera will give you a view of the  unlock panel for you to hack walk back  to the facility entrance and pass  through the CTOs gate climb up the  ladder then drop down to the area with  the forklift to access the tower  Parker Square South using the public  furniture sign as the starting points  head south and make a ride into the  first alley head into the small parking  lot with the barbed wire and forest wall  and climb up using the forklift keep  climbing until you reach the catwalk on  the right and use another lift as a  bridge to reach another part of the  building 